Package: imbsize
Type: Package
Title: Sample Size for Logistic Risk Models Fitted with or Without Rebalancing
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Rolando", "de la Cruz", email = "rolando.delacruz@uai.cl",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1415-1809"))
Description: Sample-size criteria for developing logistic risk prediction models
    fitted without rebalancing, with class weights or with random undersampling.
    Criterion C1 requires an expected calibration slope of at least S for models used
    without recalibration; criterion C2 requires that the AUC lost by estimating a model
    that will be recalibrated be at most delta. Both are computed from the
    proportional-asymptotic limits of the fit under a Gaussian model, in exact and
    closed forms and in versions that meet the target with a given probability, and
    express the cost of rebalancing as a multiplier of the required sample size.
